#PayPal(PYPL) Morningstar Deep Undervaluation Research

> Study date: May 19, 2026
> Morningstar Fair Value: $80 | Current Price: $44.38 | Potential Gain: +80.2%
> Moat Rating: Narrow Moat | Uncertainty Rating: High
> Industry: Credit Services

---

## 1. Company Profile

### Main business

PayPal is the world's leading digital payments platform, providing online and mobile payment solutions for consumers and merchants. Core products include PayPal checkout, Venmo (P2P payments), Braintree (merchant payment processing), Xoom (cross-border remittances), etc. The company was spun off from eBay in 2015 and went public independently.

### Income structure

- **Transaction revenue**: accounting for approximately 90% of total revenue, derived from merchant transaction fees (charged as a percentage of transaction amount + fixed fee)
- **Value-added service revenue**: accounting for about 10%, including merchant and consumer financial services (loans, interest income, etc.). In 2025, this part of the revenue will be approximately US$3.4 billion.

### Market position

- The global online payment processing market share is approximately 41%-45%, significantly ahead of Stripe (approximately 8%)
- Approximately 439 million active accounts in 2025
- Total payment volume (TPV) in 2025 will reach US$1.79 trillion, a year-on-year increase of 7%
- The top 60% of the world’s top e-commerce websites offer PayPal checkout option

